  "_note": "The Gold Souk in Al Ras, Deira (src/components/arcade/games/goldsouk). Gold is sold by weight at the day's rate for its carat, plus a making charge per gram, and bargaining is expected. The day's 24K rate moves within `swing` of `base24` (AED per gram), the same for everyone on a given day; other carats are fractions of it. Some pieces are gold-plated fakes (more at higher levels): the hallmark reads GP and the magnet test catches them. Merchants are Locals: patience is how many lowball offers they'll take, margin their lowest mark-up over the true value. Levels are the haggler ladder (buyer) or the stall's customers (trader job).",
